I'll cache the resolved field pointer bounds check into a single branch on the already-likely-valid profile pointer, avoiding the second dereference chain when profile is non-null.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG_FIELD* f = profile ? &profile->fields[profileIndex] : NULL;
    if ((f == NULL) || (profileIndex >= profile->numFields))
        return 0;
    return f->numSubFields;
}
```